<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Temryuk Idarov</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/1571">1571</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> · Also known as Temryuk of Kabarda</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Temryuk Idarov was the leading prince of Kabarda in the mid-sixteenth century. Facing the Crimean Khanate and rival princes, he sought an alliance with Muscovy, sending envoys to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ivan-iv-of-russia">Ivan IV</a> in 1557, and in 1561 his daughter Maria married the tsar. The alliance began long Russian involvement in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-caucasus">North Caucasus</a>.</p></div>
